message: "If you use this software or its associated research outputs, please cite the repository using the metadata below."

title: "Generalizable Ensemble Deep Learning for Skin Lesion Classification: Internal and External Validation on HAM10000 and ISIC 2019"

authors:
  - family-names: "Saykat"
    given-names: "Md Naim Hassan"
    affiliation: "Department of Computer Science, Université Paris-Saclay"
    email: "mdnaimhassansaykat@gmail.com"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-5270-3970"

abstract: >
  Reproducible deep learning framework for multiclass dermoscopic skin-lesion
  classification with internal validation on HAM10000 and external validation
  on ISIC 2019. The repository provides implementations and evaluation
  workflows for seven deep learning backbones spanning conventional CNNs,
  ResNet-50, DenseNet-121, EfficientNet-B3, ConvNeXt-Tiny,
  MobileNetV3-Large, and ViT-B/16, together with probability-level
  soft-voting ensemble inference. The framework includes standardized data
  preprocessing, training and evaluation pipelines, class-imbalance handling,
  model calibration, discrimination and classification metrics,
  interpretability analysis, and reproducibility artifacts for assessing
  generalization across internal and external dermoscopic datasets.

repository-code: "https://github.com/md-naim-hassan-saykat/skin-lesion-classification-ensemble-ham10000"

